The intent of this Ordinance is to promote the health, safety, morals, convenience, order, prosperity, and general welfare of the present and future inhabitants of the County. In furtherance of this general intent, the regulation of land development by Taliaferro County, Georgia is adopted for the following purposes:
1. To secure safety from fire, panic and other dangers;
2. To promote the health and general welfare;
3. To provide adequate light and air;
4. To provide adequate water, sewerage and surface drainage;
5. To assure the timely provision of public facilities and services to new land development;
6. To protect property against blight and depreciation;
7. To encourage the efficient use of land and structures; and
8. To assure the adequate provision of safe and convenient traffic access and circulation, both vehicular and pedestrian, in and through new land development.

